  "term": "T-squared test",
  "definition": "A T-squared test, in this context, is a statistical test used to determine whether an observed brain response is significantly locked to a repeating visual stimulus. Here, the circular Hotelling’s T-squared test was used to show that many participants had strong stimulus-synchronized visual evoked responses.",
