      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims the test determines whether an observed brain response is “significantly locked to a repeating visual stimulus.” The packet supports “significantly strong stimulus-locked SSMVEP responses,” but it does not explicitly describe the stimulus as “repeating” (beyond mentioning tested frequencies in the motion reversal protocol).",
        "While the packet supports that “Circular Hotelling’s T-squared test” demonstrated most subjects had significantly strong stimulus-locked responses, the definition’s wording “many participants had strong stimulus-synchronized visual evoked responses” is a paraphrase that introduces “stimulus-synchronized” and “participants” without direct phrasing support (though the underlying meaning is close)."
